[ti:There Used To Be a Brighter Boy]
[ar:Ash Stu]
[al:Ash Stu, Vol. I]
[re:aligned with Demucs vocal separation + MMS forced alignment, cross-checked with Whisper alignment; edit timestamps by hand if a line is off]
[00:00.92]There used to be a brighter boy
[00:05.80]With pockets full of tinker toys
[00:11.55]Who liked to say that he could spell his name
[00:19.54]He let his room become a mess
[00:24.80]He made his hair a blind bird's nest
[00:29.78]He tangled up the earbuds in his pocket
[00:36.65]So then he grinned a bit too wide
[00:40.25]And wore his pants a bit too high
[00:44.02]And stuffed the floor into his dresser drawer
[00:47.80]And now he has to float around
[00:51.30]And squint real hard to see the ground
[00:54.96]And bump between the corners of his walls
[00:57.57]He pulls the string of a balloon
[01:01.13]And paddles air with a silver spoon
[01:03.99]And sometimes sings a song to spend his time
